# Orders (planned — not built)

Auth and tenancy foundation exists (`accounts`, `branches`). Use when implementing orders.

@docs/warehouse-tenancy-setup.md

## Already in place

- `accounts.User` — email login
- `Branch`, `BranchMembership` — roles per branch
- `branches/permissions.py` — `can_create_order`, `can_edit_or_delete_order`, etc.
- `request.active_branch` — session-based active branch

## Order phase rules

- Every `Order` has required `branch` FK and `created_by` FK
- Always query orders via branch-scoped manager (e.g. `.for_user_branches(user)`)
- Role checks at view entry using `branches/permissions.py`
- Client-side order IDs for idempotent sync (offline retries)
- Product catalogue stays global (no `branch_id` on `Product`)
